% The spending paths of the policy.
rule decaying_threshold with provenance the Bitcoin Core descriptor documentation,
        confer "and finally 1-of-4 at each future halvening block height":
the coin can be spent if
    a number N is the count of each C such that
        a condition C is in [the signature of key 1, the signature of key 2, the signature of key 3, the signature of key 4, the lock at block 840000, the lock at block 1050000, the lock at block 1260000]
        and the condition C is met
    and N >= 4.

rule decaying_threshold_condition_1 with provenance the Bitcoin Core descriptor documentation,
        confer "and finally 1-of-4 at each future halvening block height":
the condition the signature of key 1 is met if
    the witness contains a signature by key 1.

rule decaying_threshold_condition_2 with provenance the Bitcoin Core descriptor documentation,
        confer "and finally 1-of-4 at each future halvening block height":
the condition the signature of key 2 is met if
    the witness contains a signature by key 2.

rule decaying_threshold_condition_3 with provenance the Bitcoin Core descriptor documentation,
        confer "and finally 1-of-4 at each future halvening block height":
the condition the signature of key 3 is met if
    the witness contains a signature by key 3.

rule decaying_threshold_condition_4 with provenance the Bitcoin Core descriptor documentation,
        confer "and finally 1-of-4 at each future halvening block height":
the condition the signature of key 4 is met if
    the witness contains a signature by key 4.

rule decaying_threshold_condition_5 with provenance the Bitcoin Core descriptor documentation,
        confer "and finally 1-of-4 at each future halvening block height":
the condition the lock at block 840000 is met if
    the spending transaction has the lock time a number N
    and the lock time N is a block height
    and N >= 840000
    and the spending transaction is in block a height H
    and N < H.

rule decaying_threshold_condition_6 with provenance the Bitcoin Core descriptor documentation,
        confer "and finally 1-of-4 at each future halvening block height":
the condition the lock at block 1050000 is met if
    the spending transaction has the lock time a number N
    and the lock time N is a block height
    and N >= 1050000
    and the spending transaction is in block a height H
    and N < H.

rule decaying_threshold_condition_7 with provenance the Bitcoin Core descriptor documentation,
        confer "and finally 1-of-4 at each future halvening block height":
the condition the lock at block 1260000 is met if
    the spending transaction has the lock time a number N
    and the lock time N is a block height
    and N >= 1260000
    and the spending transaction is in block a height H
    and N < H.

